"""Original-host launch and recovery help after retiring the third-party window."""
from play_recommendations import recommendations, stylesheet

P = '/azeroth-survivors/'
GAME = 'https://s.the-false-sun.com/azeroth-survivors/index.html'


def play_page(shell, ext):
    body = f'''<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="{P}">Azeroth Survivors</a> / Play</nav>
<header class="article-head" id="guide"><h1>Play Azeroth Survivors online</h1><div class="answer"><p>Open <strong>Aethus’s original Azeroth Survivors at wow.aethus.pl</strong> in a new tab. Keep this page open for startup help and save precautions.</p></div><p class="meta">Megabonk.org · Updated 5 November 2026 · Original-host launch guide</p><div class="actions">{ext('https://wow.aethus.pl/','Aethus · open the original game')}</div></header>
<div class="article-layout"><aside class="toc" aria-label="Play help"><a href="#start">Start on the original site</a><a href="#rendering">Missing text or icons</a><a href="#edition">Keep your saves</a><a href="#loading">Startup help</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></aside><article class="prose">
<section id="start"><h2>Start on Aethus’s original site</h2><ol><li>Use the original-game link above. Check that the destination is <strong>wow.aethus.pl</strong>.</li><li>Keep that game tab open while its resources and world data prepare. Read any graphics-support message in the game.</li><li>Choose your character and zone in the client. The <a href="{P}beginners-guide/">beginner guide</a> explains the version-labelled first-run choices.</li><li>Click inside the game for keyboard focus and use its input settings. Keep the guide in this tab when you need help.</li></ol><p>The original client checks its host and blocks third-party frames. Its entry therefore opens in a separate tab.<sup class="ref"><a href="#source-1">[1]</a></sup> The screenshot below records an earlier original-client menu, with its version and capture date.</p></section>
<section id="rendering"><h2>Square text or empty spell pictures in the previous window?</h2><p>On 5 November 2026 a visitor reported square text and empty spell-card pictures in our former third-party game window. That provider’s startup page explicitly documents a client font without CJK glyphs, which can display Chinese text as boxes. Its page attempts to force English at boot. The exact cause of the empty spell pictures remains unconfirmed.<sup class="ref"><a href="#source-2">[2]</a></sup></p><p>We retired that window and now direct the main Play entry to Aethus’s original site. The third-party client’s font and texture rendering remain outside this guide’s control.</p><p>If you need an old session, keep the same browser profile and host while backing it up. If its settings remain readable, try selecting English inside that client. Export progress before clearing site data or reinstalling anything.</p></section>
<section id="edition"><h2>Protect progress before changing hosts</h2><p>The former window used <strong>s.the-false-sun.com</strong>, a separate provider. Its menu displayed v0.90.0 on 31 October. Our original-client screenshot records v0.130.0 on 30 October. These historical captures do not establish current versions.<sup class="ref"><a href="#source-2">[2]</a></sup><sup class="ref"><a href="#source-3">[3]</a></sup></p><ol><li>Keep the old address, browser profile and existing site data. {ext(GAME,'s.the-false-sun.com · old-host save recovery')} opens the former provider separately; the reported rendering fault may still occur.</li><li>If that client offers a save export, keep an unchanged copy. We cannot read its cross-origin storage. A separate tab may have different storage access from a framed session.</li><li>In the original client, use <strong>Options → Saves → Export Save</strong> to back up existing progress before trying an import.</li><li>Import replaces progress. Keep both originals and check the <a href="{P}save-backup/">original-game backup guide</a> first. Transfer between these clients has not been verified.</li></ol><p>Opening either external game connects to its provider and services. See the <a href="/privacy-policy#azeroth-survivors-guides">game-link privacy notice</a>.</p></section>
<section id="loading"><h2>If the original game does not start</h2><p>Read the client’s support message first. Its launcher checks WebGPU and device limits before booting. Our <a href="{P}troubleshooting/">startup troubleshooting</a> separates graphics support, preparation and save issues.<sup class="ref"><a href="#source-1">[1]</a></sup></p><p>Allow initial world-data preparation to finish. Repeated reloads start a new page session. Keep the actual game tab open during play and use its own pause control before switching away.</p><p>For phones, graphics support, touch controls and persistent storage are separate checks. See <a href="{P}mobile/">browser and mobile requirements</a> or <a href="{P}download-platforms/">platform choices</a>. Responsive-page checks do not establish physical-phone compatibility or a full gameplay session.</p></section>
<section class="sources" id="sources"><h2>Sources &amp; verification</h2><ol><li id="source-1">{ext('https://wow.aethus.pl/rogue.js?v=f3a3d645a1ed','Aethus · original launcher source')} — checked 5 November 2026. Host/frame gates, WebGPU checks and save controls. Source inspection and navigation checks; no new full-run benchmark.</li><li id="source-2">{ext(GAME,'s.the-false-sun.com · former game host')} — startup HTML read 5 November 2026. Its comment documents missing CJK glyphs and an English boot override. The visitor’s card screenshot shows missing pictures; the failed texture or rendering stage has not been established. The v0.90.0 menu was captured 31 October.</li><li id="source-3">{ext('https://wow.aethus.pl/','Aethus · original game')} — original v0.130.0 menu captured 30 October 2026. Used to identify the original character, equipment and zone screen. Game art © respective owners.</li></ol><a href="#guide">Back to play ↑</a></section>
<section class="related"><h2>Plan your next choice</h2><a href="{P}beginners-guide/">Original-game first run →</a><a href="{P}builds/">Class build routes →</a><a href="{P}save-backup/">Keep a save backup →</a></section></article></div>{recommendations('azeroth-survivors')}'''
    html = shell(P+'play/', 'Play Azeroth Survivors Online | Megabonk.org', 'Open Azeroth Survivors on Aethus’s original site. Find startup help, missing-text and icon guidance, and save precautions before changing clients.', body)
    return P+'play/', stylesheet(html).replace('</head>', '<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/azeroth-survivors/play.css"></head>', 1)
